-- Code of Practice for General-Purpose AI Models, Safety and Security Chapter.
-- Commitment 9 (serious incident reporting), Measures 9.1 to 9.4, with the Code's
-- status and the Glossary terms Commitment 9 uses.
--
-- DRAFT. Not for use as advice. No domain expert and no lawyer qualified in EU law
-- has read this against the source.
--
-- Seat: the provider (a Signatory, or a provider deciding whether the Code binds it).
-- Source: ../../registers/source-bundle/cop-safety-security-2025.txt; `src:N` is line N.
-- Page numbers in the @refs are the printed page numbers, which equal the PDF's.
-- Target compiler: main. Forks F1 to F15 are in NOTES.md.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cop-domain`

§ `The Code's status: whom it binds`

-- src:28 | To achieve this overarching objective, the specific objectives of this Code are:
-- src:30 | A. To serve as a guiding document for demonstrating compliance with the obligations provided
-- src:31 | for in Articles 53 and 55 AI Act, while recognising that adherence to the Code does not
-- src:32 | constitute conclusive evidence of compliance with these obligations under the AI Act.
-- src:34 | B. To ensure providers of general-purpose AI models comply with their obligations under the AI
-- src:35 | Act and to enable the AI Office to assess compliance of providers of general-purpose AI
-- src:36 | models who choose to rely on the Code to demonstrate compliance with their obligations
-- src:37 | under the AI Act.
-- Objective A says what adherence does NOT prove. Nothing in the Chapter says what
-- follows for a provider who does not adhere, and this encoding says nothing about it.
@ref Objectives, points A and B, p. 2 (src:28-37)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`adhering to the Code is conclusive evidence of compliance with Articles 53 and 55 AI Act` MEANS
    FALSE

-- src:62 | (b) Principle of Contextual Risk Assessment and Mitigation. The Signatories recognise that this
-- src:63 | Safety and Security Chapter (“Chapter”) is only relevant for providers of general-purpose AI
-- src:64 | models with systemic risk and not AI systems. However, the Signatories also recognise that
-- src:1230 | ‘model’ a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk.
-- The Chapter's duties are written as "Signatories commit to" and "Signatories will"
-- (for Commitment 9, src:991); it never defines "Signatory" and never says how a provider
-- becomes one (F1). Both facts are the provider's to state.
@ref Recital (b), p. 3 (src:62-64); Glossary 'model', p. 30 (src:1230)
DECLARE `does the Chapter bind me` IS ONE OF
    `the Chapter binds me`
    `the Chapter does not bind me, because I am not a Signatory`
    `the Chapter is not relevant here, because the model is not a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk`

@ref Recital (b), p. 3 (src:62-64); Glossary 'model', p. 30 (src:1230)
GIVEN s IS A `the provider's standing`
GIVETH A `does the Chapter bind me`
`whether the Chapter binds me` s MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT s's `I am a Signatory of the Chapter`)
            THEN `the Chapter does not bind me, because I am not a Signatory`
        IF (NOT s's `the model involved is a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk`)
            THEN `the Chapter is not relevant here, because the model is not a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk`
        OTHERWISE `the Chapter binds me`

@ref Recital (b), p. 3 (src:62-64)
GIVEN s IS A `the provider's standing`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Commitment 9 applies to me` s MEANS
    CONSIDER `whether the Chapter binds me` s
    WHEN `the Chapter binds me` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- Recital (h) is inert here: it says SMEs and SMCs "may be exempted from some reporting
-- commitments (Article 56(5) AI Act)" and does not say which (F2).
-- src:129 | (h) Small and medium enterprises (“SMEs”) and small mid-cap enterprises (“SMCs”). To
-- src:130 | account for differences between providers of general-purpose AI models with systemic risk
-- src:131 | regarding their size and capacity, simplified ways of compliance for SMEs and SMCs, including
-- src:132 | startups, should be possible as proportionate. For example, SMEs and SMCs may be
-- src:133 | exempted from some reporting commitments (Article 56(5) AI Act). Signatories that are SMEs
-- src:134 | or SMCs and are exempted from reporting commitments recognise that they may
-- src:135 | nonetheless voluntarily adhere to them.

-- Recital (j) is inert: it says why, and that a report "is not an admission of wrongdoing".
-- src:153 | (j) Serious Incident Reporting. The Signatories recognise that the reporting of a serious incident
-- src:154 | is not an admission of wrongdoing. Further, they recognise that relevant information about
-- src:155 | serious incidents cannot be kept track of, documented, and reported at the model level only
-- src:156 | in retrospect after a serious incident has occurred. The information that could directly or
-- src:157 | indirectly lead up to such an event is often dispersed and may be lost, overwritten, or
-- src:158 | fragmented by the time Signatories become aware of a serious incident. This justifies the
-- src:159 | establishment of processes and measures to keep track of and document relevant
-- src:160 | information before serious incidents occur.

-- 'serious incident' is NOT defined in the Chapter's Glossary. The Glossary says a term
-- defined in Article 3 AI Act takes that definition (F3); the AI Act is not deposited
-- in this subject. Measure 9.3 names the harms that start each clock, so this encoding
-- asks about those harms and does not restate the AI Act's definition.
-- src:1136 | Glossary
-- src:1137 | Wherever this Chapter refers to a term defined in Article 3 AI Act, the AI Act definition applies, and
-- src:1138 | such definition shall prevail in the event of any alternative and/or competing interpretation to which
-- src:1139 | the use of the term in this Chapter may give rise. Otherwise and complementing this, the following
-- src:1140 | terms with the stated meanings are used in this Chapter. Unless otherwise stated, all grammatical
-- src:1141 | variations of the terms defined in this Glossary shall be deemed to be covered by the relevant
-- src:1142 | definition.

§ `Commitment 9 -- Serious incident reporting`

-- The chapeau is inert: "without undue delay" and resourcing "appropriate for the
-- severity" are not computed (F4). The Measures below give the outer limits.
-- src:988 | Commitment 9 Serious incident reporting
-- src:989 | LEGAL TEXT: Article 55(1), and recitals 114 and 115 AI Act
-- src:991 | Signatories commit to implementing appropriate processes and measures for keeping track of,
-- src:992 | documenting, and reporting to the AI Office and, as applicable, to national competent authorities,
-- src:993 | without undue delay relevant information about serious incidents along the entire model lifecycle
-- src:994 | and possible corrective measures to address them, as specified in the Measures of this Commitment.
-- src:995 | Further, Signatories commit to providing resourcing of such processes and measures appropriate for
-- src:996 | the severity of the serious incident and the degree of involvement of their model.

§ `Measure 9.1 -- Methods for serious incident identification`

-- src:998 | Measure 9.1 Methods for serious incident identification
-- src:999 | Signatories will consider the exemplary methods in Measure 3.5 to keep track of relevant information
-- src:1000 | about serious incidents. Additionally, Signatories will:
-- src:1001 | (1) review other sources of information, such as police and media reports, posts on social media,
-- src:1002 | research papers, and incident databases; and
-- src:1008 | (2) facilitate the reporting of relevant information about serious incidents by downstream
-- src:1009 | modifiers, downstream providers, users, and other third parties to:
-- src:1010 | (a) the Signatory; or
-- src:1011 | (b) the AI Office and, as applicable, national competent authorities;
-- src:1012 | by informing such third parties of direct reporting channels, if available, without prejudice to
-- src:1013 | any of their reporting obligations under Article 73 AI Act.
-- Point (2) names one means, "informing ... of direct reporting channels, if available".
-- Where no channel is available the Measure names no other means, so the encoding
-- treats point (2) as met (F5).
@ref Measure 9.1, pp. 25-26 (src:998-1013)
GIVEN m IS A `my incident identification`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I meet Measure 9.1` m IF
        m's `I consider the exemplary methods in Measure 3.5`
    AND m's `I review other sources such as police and media reports, social media, research papers and incident databases`
    AND (   (NOT m's `direct reporting channels are available`)
         OR m's `I inform third parties of the direct reporting channels`)

§ `Measure 9.2 -- Relevant information for serious incident tracking, documentation, and reporting`

-- src:1015 | Measure 9.2 Relevant information for serious incident tracking, documentation, and
-- src:1016 | reporting
-- src:1017 | Signatories will keep track of, document, and report to the AI Office and, as applicable, to national
-- src:1018 | competent authorities, at least the following information to the best of their knowledge, redacted
-- src:1019 | to the extent necessary to comply with other Union law applicable to such information:
-- src:1020 | (1) the start and end dates of the serious incident, or best approximations thereof if the precise
-- src:1021 | dates are unclear;
-- src:1022 | (2) the resulting harm and the victim or affected group of the serious incident;
-- src:1023 | (3) the chain of events that (directly or indirectly) led to the serious incident;
-- src:1024 | (4) the model involved in the serious incident;
-- src:1025 | (5) a description of material available setting out the model’s involvement in the serious incident;
-- src:1026 | (6) what, if anything, the Signatory intends to do or has done in response to the serious incident;
-- src:1027 | (7) what, if anything, the Signatory recommends the AI Office and, as applicable, national
-- src:1028 | competent authorities to do in response to the serious incident;
-- src:1029 | (8) a root cause analysis with a description of the model’s outputs that (directly or indirectly) led
-- src:1030 | to the serious incident and the factors that contributed to their generation, including the
-- src:1031 | inputs used and any failures or circumventions of systemic risk mitigations; and
-- src:1032 | (9) any patterns detected during post-market monitoring (pursuant to Measure 3.5) that can
-- src:1033 | reasonably be assumed to be connected to the serious incident, such as individual or
-- src:1034 | aggregate data on near misses.
@ref Measure 9.2, first paragraph, p. 26 (src:1015-1034)
GIVETH A LIST OF `an item of Measure 9.2`
`every item of Measure 9.2` MEANS
    LIST `item 1, start and end dates`
       , `item 2, resulting harm and victims`
       , `item 3, chain of events`
       , `item 4, model involved`
       , `item 5, material on the model's involvement`
       , `item 6, what I intend to do or have done`
       , `item 7, what I recommend the authorities do`
       , `item 8, root cause analysis`
       , `item 9, patterns from post-market monitoring`

-- The second paragraph: an item not yet held is recorded as such in the report.
-- The investigation duty and "level of detail ... appropriate for the severity" are not
-- computed.
-- src:1036 | Signatories will investigate the causes and effects of serious incidents, including the information
-- src:1037 | within the preceding list, with a view to informing systemic risk assessment. If Signatories do not yet
-- src:1038 | have certain relevant information from the preceding list, they will record that in their serious
-- src:1039 | incident reports. The level of detail in serious incident reports will be appropriate for the severity of
-- src:1040 | the incident.
@ref Measure 9.2, second paragraph, p. 26 (src:1036-1040)
GIVEN `the required items`         IS A LIST OF `an item of Measure 9.2`
      `the items the report gives` IS A LIST OF `an item of Measure 9.2`
      `the items the report records as not yet held` IS A LIST OF `an item of Measure 9.2`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the report accounts for every required item` `the required items` `the items the report gives` `the items the report records as not yet held` MEANS
    all (GIVEN item YIELD    elem item `the items the report gives`
                          OR elem item `the items the report records as not yet held`)
        `the required items`

§ `Measure 9.3 -- Reporting timelines`

§§ `Measure 9.3, initial report`

-- src:1042 | Measure 9.3 Reporting timelines
-- src:1043 | Signatories will provide the information in points (1) to (7) of Measure 9.2 in an initial report that is
-- src:1044 | submitted to the AI Office and, as applicable, to national competent authorities, at the following
-- src:1045 | points in time, save in exceptional circumstances, if the involvement of their model (directly or
-- src:1046 | indirectly) led to:
@ref Measure 9.3, first paragraph, p. 26 (src:1042-1046)
GIVETH A LIST OF `an item of Measure 9.2`
`the items an initial report must give` MEANS
    LIST `item 1, start and end dates`
       , `item 2, resulting harm and victims`
       , `item 3, chain of events`
       , `item 4, model involved`
       , `item 5, material on the model's involvement`
       , `item 6, what I intend to do or have done`
       , `item 7, what I recommend the authorities do`

-- The two routes each point names: the model's involvement "led to" the harm, or the
-- Signatory "establish[es] or suspect[s] with reasonable likelihood such a causal
-- relationship". Either brings the harm within the point.
@ref Measure 9.3, first paragraph, p. 26 (src:1045-1046)
GIVEN l IS A `my model's link to a harm`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the link brings the harm within Measure 9.3` l MEANS
    CONSIDER l
    WHEN `my model's involvement led to it, directly or indirectly`                   THEN TRUE
    WHEN `I establish or suspect with reasonable likelihood that my model caused it` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `no such harm, or no link to my model`                                       THEN FALSE

-- Days are counted as calendar days after the date of awareness, that date excluded;
-- a report on the last day is in time (F6). The clock runs from awareness of the
-- MODEL'S INVOLVEMENT, not from the incident (F7).
-- src:1047 | (1) a serious and irreversible disruption of the management or operation of critical
-- src:1048 | infrastructure, or if the Signatories establish or suspect with reasonable likelihood such a
-- src:1049 | causal relationship between their model and the disruption, not later than two days after the
-- src:1050 | Signatories become aware of the involvement of their model in the incident;
@ref Measure 9.3, first paragraph, point (1), p. 26 (src:1047-1050)
GIVEN i IS A `the incident as I know it`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `point 1 applies to` i IF
    `the link brings the harm within Measure 9.3` (i's `link to a serious and irreversible disruption of the management or operation of critical infrastructure`)

@ref Measure 9.3, first paragraph, point (1), p. 26 (src:1049-1050)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days point 1 allows` MEANS 2

-- "including" introduces the minimum the term covers (Glossary, p. 29), so the
-- (self-)exfiltration of model weights and cyberattacks are within point (2) (F8).
-- src:1055 | (2) a serious cybersecurity breach, including the (self-)exfiltration of model weights and
-- src:1056 | cyberattacks, or if the Signatories establish or suspect with reasonable likelihood such a
-- src:1057 | causal relationship between their model and the breach, not later than five days after the
-- src:1058 | Signatories become aware of the involvement of their model in the incident;
-- src:1180 | ‘including’ introduces a non-exhaustive set that is to be understood as the minimum
-- src:1181 | required by the term referred to and is indicative of further items of the set.
-- src:1315 | ‘(self-)exfiltration access or transfer of weights or associated assets of a model from their secure
-- src:1316 | of model weights’ storage by the model itself and/or an unauthorised actor.
@ref Measure 9.3, first paragraph, point (2), p. 27 (src:1055-1058); Glossary 'including', p. 29, and '(self-)exfiltration of model weights', p. 32 (src:1180-1181) (src:1315-1316)
GIVEN i IS A `the incident as I know it`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `point 2 applies to` i IF
    `the link brings the harm within Measure 9.3` (i's `link to a serious cybersecurity breach`)

@ref Measure 9.3, first paragraph, point (2), p. 27 (src:1057-1058)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days point 2 allows` MEANS 5

-- src:1059 | (3) a death of a person, or if the Signatories establish or suspect with reasonable likelihood such
-- src:1060 | a causal relationship between their model and the death, not later than 10 days after the
-- src:1061 | Signatories become aware of the involvement of their model in the incident; and
@ref Measure 9.3, first paragraph, point (3), p. 27 (src:1059-1061)
GIVEN i IS A `the incident as I know it`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `point 3 applies to` i IF
    `the link brings the harm within Measure 9.3` (i's `link to the death of a person`)

@ref Measure 9.3, first paragraph, point (3), p. 27 (src:1060-1061)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days point 3 allows` MEANS 10

-- src:1062 | (4) serious harm to a person’s health (mental and/or physical), an infringement of obligations
-- src:1063 | under Union law intended to protect fundamental rights, and/or serious harm to property or
-- src:1064 | the environment, or if the Signatories establish or suspect with reasonable likelihood such a
-- src:1065 | causal relationship between their model and the harms or infringements, not later than 15
-- src:1066 | days after the Signatories become aware of the involvement of their model in the incident.
@ref Measure 9.3, first paragraph, point (4), p. 27 (src:1062-1066)
GIVEN i IS A `the incident as I know it`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `point 4 applies to` i IF
       `the link brings the harm within Measure 9.3` (i's `link to serious harm to a person's health`)
    OR `the link brings the harm within Measure 9.3` (i's `link to an infringement of Union-law obligations that protect fundamental rights`)
    OR `the link brings the harm within Measure 9.3` (i's `link to serious harm to property`)
    OR `the link brings the harm within Measure 9.3` (i's `link to serious harm to the environment`)

@ref Measure 9.3, first paragraph, point (4), p. 27 (src:1065-1066)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days point 4 allows` MEANS 15

@ref Measure 9.3, first paragraph, points (1) to (4), pp. 26-27
GIVEN p IS A `a point of Measure 9.3`, i IS A `the incident as I know it`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the point applies to the incident` p i MEANS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `point 1, critical infrastructure`                             THEN `point 1 applies to` i
    WHEN `point 2, cybersecurity breach`                                THEN `point 2 applies to` i
    WHEN `point 3, death`                                               THEN `point 3 applies to` i
    WHEN `point 4, health, fundamental rights, property or environment` THEN `point 4 applies to` i

@ref Measure 9.3, first paragraph, points (1) to (4), pp. 26-27
GIVEN p IS A `a point of Measure 9.3`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days the point allows` p MEANS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `point 1, critical infrastructure`                             THEN `the days point 1 allows`
    WHEN `point 2, cybersecurity breach`                                THEN `the days point 2 allows`
    WHEN `point 3, death`                                               THEN `the days point 3 allows`
    WHEN `point 4, health, fundamental rights, property or environment` THEN `the days point 4 allows`

@ref Measure 9.3, first paragraph, points (1) to (4), pp. 26-27
GIVEN p IS A `a point of Measure 9.3`, i IS A `the incident as I know it`
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to report under the point` p i MEANS
    i's `the date I became aware of my model's involvement in the incident` PLUS `the days the point allows` p

-- One clock for each point that applies. The Code does not say which clock governs
-- when more than one point applies (F9): the answer below gives every clock that
-- applies, the earliest of them (reading R-A: each point binds on its own, so one
-- report by the earliest date meets all of them) and the latest (the outer bound if
-- only one clock were to govern, reading R-B, which the Code does not name).
DECLARE `an applicable clock` HAS
    `the point that sets the clock` IS A `a point of Measure 9.3`
    `the last day the clock allows` IS A DATE

@ref Measure 9.3, first paragraph, points (1) to (4), pp. 26-27
GIVEN i IS A `the incident as I know it`
GIVETH A LIST OF `an applicable clock`
`the clocks of the points that apply to` i MEANS
    map (GIVEN p YIELD `an applicable clock` WITH `the point that sets the clock` IS p
                                                  `the last day the clock allows` IS `the last day to report under the point` p i)
        (filter (GIVEN p YIELD `the point applies to the incident` p i)
                (LIST `point 1, critical infrastructure`
                    , `point 2, cybersecurity breach`
                    , `point 3, death`
                    , `point 4, health, fundamental rights, property or environment`))

GIVEN d IS A DATE, cs IS A LIST OF `an applicable clock`
GIVETH A DATE
`the earliest last day, from` d `and` cs MEANS
    CONSIDER cs
    WHEN EMPTY THEN d
    WHEN c FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        IF c's `the last day the clock allows` AT MOST d
        THEN `the earliest last day, from` (c's `the last day the clock allows`) `and` rest
        ELSE `the earliest last day, from` d `and` rest

GIVEN d IS A DATE, cs IS A LIST OF `an applicable clock`
GIVETH A DATE
`the latest last day, from` d `and` cs MEANS
    CONSIDER cs
    WHEN EMPTY THEN d
    WHEN c FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        IF c's `the last day the clock allows` AT LEAST d
        THEN `the latest last day, from` (c's `the last day the clock allows`) `and` rest
        ELSE `the latest last day, from` d `and` rest

-- "save in exceptional circumstances": the Code does not define them and sets no other
-- time for them, so the provider states whether they apply and the encoding then gives
-- no date (F10). It is never guessed.
-- The two reasons for no duty at all follow `whether the Chapter binds me`, so each
-- answer below gives the same reason the "Does this Code bind me?" question gives.
DECLARE `when my initial report is due` IS ONE OF
    `no initial report is due, because the Chapter does not bind me`
    `no initial report is due, because the model is not a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk`
    `no initial report is due under Measure 9.3, because none of its points applies`
    `the Code sets no deadline, because exceptional circumstances apply`
    `report by the last day one point allows` HAS
        `the one clock that applies` IS AN `an applicable clock`
    `more than one point applies, and the Code does not say which clock governs` HAS
        `every clock that applies`                    IS A LIST OF `an applicable clock`
        `the earliest last day, if every clock binds` IS A DATE
        `the latest last day among them`              IS A DATE

@ref Measure 9.3, first paragraph, pp. 26-27, "save in exceptional circumstances"
GIVEN s IS A `the provider's standing`, i IS A `the incident as I know it`
GIVETH A `when my initial report is due`
`when my initial report is due under Measure 9.3` s i MEANS
    CONSIDER `whether the Chapter binds me` s
    WHEN `the Chapter does not bind me, because I am not a Signatory`
        THEN `no initial report is due, because the Chapter does not bind me`
    WHEN `the Chapter is not relevant here, because the model is not a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk`
        THEN `no initial report is due, because the model is not a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk`
    WHEN `the Chapter binds me` THEN
        CONSIDER `the clocks of the points that apply to` i
        WHEN EMPTY THEN `no initial report is due under Measure 9.3, because none of its points applies`
        WHEN c FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
            IF i's `exceptional circumstances apply`
            THEN `the Code sets no deadline, because exceptional circumstances apply`
            ELSE CONSIDER rest
                 WHEN EMPTY THEN `report by the last day one point allows` c
                 OTHERWISE `more than one point applies, and the Code does not say which clock governs` WITH
                     `every clock that applies`                    IS c FOLLOWED BY rest
                     `the earliest last day, if every clock binds` IS `the earliest last day, from` (c's `the last day the clock allows`) `and` rest
                     `the latest last day among them`              IS `the latest last day, from` (c's `the last day the clock allows`) `and` rest

-- A report is in time if it is submitted on or before the last day (F6).
@ref Measure 9.3, "not later than", pp. 26-27
GIVEN `the day it was submitted` IS A DATE, `the last day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`submitted in time` `the day it was submitted` `the last day` MEANS
    `the day it was submitted` AT MOST `the last day`

§§ `Measure 9.3, intermediate reports`

-- Reading taken (F11): "at least every four weeks after the initial report" means no
-- more than 28 days may pass between one report and the next, so the next intermediate
-- report is due 28 days after the latest report made (the initial report, or the latest
-- intermediate report if one was made later). Only "unresolved" incidents need one.
-- src:1068 | For unresolved serious incidents, Signatories will update the information in their initial report and
-- src:1069 | add further information required by Measure 9.2, as available, in an intermediate report that is
-- src:1070 | submitted to the AI Office and, as applicable, to national competent authorities, at least every four
-- src:1071 | weeks after the initial report.
@ref Measure 9.3, second paragraph, p. 27 (src:1068-1071)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days between intermediate reports` MEANS 28

-- 'resolved' is worked out from what the provider did (F12): corrective measures to
-- assess and mitigate the related systemic risks, and, where rectifying the harm is
-- possible, corrective measures to rectify it. The incident is resolved on the later
-- of the dates on which those measures were adopted.
-- src:1307 | ‘resolved’ (serious a serious incident of a model for which the Signatory adopted corrective
-- src:1308 | incident) measures to rectify the harm, if possible, and to assess and mitigate systemic risks
-- src:1309 | related to it. ‘Unresolved’ is to be understood accordingly.
@ref Glossary 'resolved (serious incident)', p. 32 (src:1307-1309)
GIVEN c IS A `my corrective measures`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the date the incident was resolved` c MEANS
    CONSIDER c's `the date I adopted corrective measures to assess and mitigate the related systemic risks`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST r THEN
        IF c's `rectifying the harm is possible`
        THEN CONSIDER c's `the date I adopted corrective measures to rectify the harm`
             WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
             WHEN JUST h THEN IF h AT LEAST r THEN JUST h ELSE JUST r
        ELSE JUST r

DECLARE `when my next intermediate report is due` IS ONE OF
    `no intermediate report is due, because the Chapter does not bind me`
    `no intermediate report is due, because the model is not a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk`
    `no intermediate report is due yet, because I have made no initial report`
    `no intermediate report is due, because the incident was resolved by the day it would fall due`
    `my next intermediate report is due by` HAS
        `the last day for my next intermediate report` IS A DATE

@ref Measure 9.3, second paragraph, p. 27
GIVEN s IS A `the provider's standing`
      `the date of my initial report` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date of my latest intermediate report` IS A MAYBE DATE
      c IS A `my corrective measures`
GIVETH A `when my next intermediate report is due`
`when my next intermediate report is due under Measure 9.3` s `the date of my initial report` `the date of my latest intermediate report` c MEANS
    CONSIDER `whether the Chapter binds me` s
    WHEN `the Chapter does not bind me, because I am not a Signatory`
        THEN `no intermediate report is due, because the Chapter does not bind me`
    WHEN `the Chapter is not relevant here, because the model is not a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk`
        THEN `no intermediate report is due, because the model is not a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk`
    WHEN `the Chapter binds me` THEN
        CONSIDER `the date of my initial report`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN `no intermediate report is due yet, because I have made no initial report`
        WHEN JUST initial THEN
            LET latest MEANS CONSIDER `the date of my latest intermediate report`
                             WHEN NOTHING THEN initial
                             WHEN JUST later THEN IF later AT LEAST initial THEN later ELSE initial
            IN LET due MEANS latest PLUS `the days between intermediate reports`
               IN CONSIDER `the date the incident was resolved` c
                  WHEN NOTHING THEN `my next intermediate report is due by` due
                  WHEN JUST resolved THEN
                      IF resolved AT MOST due
                      THEN `no intermediate report is due, because the incident was resolved by the day it would fall due`
                      ELSE `my next intermediate report is due by` due

§§ `Measure 9.3, final report`

-- src:1073 | Signatories will submit a final report, covering all the information required by Measure 9.2, to the AI
-- src:1074 | Office and, as applicable, to national competent authorities, not later than 60 days after the serious
-- src:1075 | incident has been resolved.
@ref Measure 9.3, third paragraph, p. 27 (src:1073-1075)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days allowed for the final report` MEANS 60

@ref Measure 9.3, third paragraph, p. 27 (src:1073-1074)
GIVETH A LIST OF `an item of Measure 9.2`
`the items a final report must give` MEANS
    `every item of Measure 9.2`

DECLARE `when my final report is due` IS ONE OF
    `no final report is due, because the Chapter does not bind me`
    `no final report is due, because the model is not a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk`
    `no final report date yet, because the incident is unresolved`
    `my final report is due by` HAS
        `the last day for my final report` IS A DATE

@ref Measure 9.3, third paragraph, p. 27 (src:1073-1075)
GIVEN s IS A `the provider's standing`, c IS A `my corrective measures`
GIVETH A `when my final report is due`
`when my final report is due under Measure 9.3` s c MEANS
    CONSIDER `whether the Chapter binds me` s
    WHEN `the Chapter does not bind me, because I am not a Signatory`
        THEN `no final report is due, because the Chapter does not bind me`
    WHEN `the Chapter is not relevant here, because the model is not a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk`
        THEN `no final report is due, because the model is not a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk`
    WHEN `the Chapter binds me` THEN
        CONSIDER `the date the incident was resolved` c
        WHEN NOTHING THEN `no final report date yet, because the incident is unresolved`
        WHEN JUST resolved THEN `my final report is due by` (resolved PLUS `the days allowed for the final report`)

@ref Measure 9.2 and Measure 9.3, first and third paragraphs, pp. 26-27
GIVEN k IS A `a report with fixed content`
GIVETH A LIST OF `an item of Measure 9.2`
`the items the report must give` k MEANS
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `an initial report` THEN `the items an initial report must give`
    WHEN `a final report`    THEN `the items a final report must give`

§§ `Measure 9.3, multiple similar serious incidents`

-- A permission. "within the reporting timelines" is not defined (F13). Two readings are
-- computed: R-A, the later incident occurred on or before the last day for the first
-- incident's initial report; R-B, it occurred while the first incident's reporting was
-- still running, that is before the last day for its final report, or at any time while
-- the first incident is unresolved. Either way the first incident's timelines still bind.
-- src:1077 | If multiple similar serious incidents occur within the reporting timelines, Signatories may include them
-- src:1078 | in the report(s) of the first serious incident, while respecting the timelines for reporting for the first
-- src:1079 | serious incident.
@ref Measure 9.3, fourth paragraph, p. 27 (src:1077-1079)
DECLARE `may I report a later similar incident with the first` HAS
    `on reading R-A, within the first incident's initial-report clock`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `on reading R-B, while the first incident's reporting is running`   IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Measure 9.3, fourth paragraph, p. 27 (src:1077-1079)
GIVEN s IS A `the provider's standing`
      `the later incident is similar to the first` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the later incident occurred` IS A DATE
      `the last day for the first incident's initial report` IS A DATE
      `the last day for the first incident's final report` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A `may I report a later similar incident with the first`
`whether I may report a later similar incident with the first` s `the later incident is similar to the first` `the date the later incident occurred` `the last day for the first incident's initial report` `the last day for the first incident's final report` MEANS
    `may I report a later similar incident with the first` WITH
        `on reading R-A, within the first incident's initial-report clock` IS
                `Commitment 9 applies to me` s
            AND `the later incident is similar to the first`
            AND `the date the later incident occurred` AT MOST `the last day for the first incident's initial report`
        `on reading R-B, while the first incident's reporting is running` IS
                `Commitment 9 applies to me` s
            AND `the later incident is similar to the first`
            AND (CONSIDER `the last day for the first incident's final report`
                 WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
                 WHEN JUST final THEN `the date the later incident occurred` AT MOST final)

§ `Measure 9.4 -- Retention period`

-- "the date of the serious incident" is one date, while Measure 9.2, point (1) gives an
-- incident a start and an end date. The Code does not say which (F14), so both are
-- computed. "five years" is counted as the same calendar date five years on; from
-- 29 February the library gives 28 February, which is the encoding's choice, not the
-- Code's (F15). "at least": this is the earliest day the documentation may be discarded.
-- src:1081 | Measure 9.4 Retention period
-- src:1082 | Signatories will keep documentation of all relevant information gathered in adhering to this
-- src:1083 | Commitment for at least five years from the date of the documentation or the date of the serious
-- src:1084 | incident, whichever is later, without prejudice to Union law applicable to such information.
@ref Measure 9.4, p. 27 (src:1081-1084)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the years documentation is kept` MEANS 5

@ref Measure 9.4, p. 27 (src:1083-1084)
GIVEN `the date of the documentation` IS A DATE, `the date of the serious incident` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the retention runs until` `the date of the documentation` `the date of the serious incident` MEANS
    IF `the date of the documentation` AT LEAST `the date of the serious incident`
    THEN `add years` `the date of the documentation` `the years documentation is kept`
    ELSE `add years` `the date of the serious incident` `the years documentation is kept`

DECLARE `how long I must keep the documentation` IS ONE OF
    `no retention duty, because the Chapter does not bind me`
    `no retention duty, because the model is not a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk`
    `keep it at least until` HAS
        `the day, if the incident's date is the day it started` IS A DATE
        `the day, if the incident's date is the day it ended`   IS A DATE

@ref Measure 9.4, p. 27 (src:1083-1084); Measure 9.2, point (1), p. 26
GIVEN s IS A `the provider's standing`
      `the date of the documentation` IS A DATE
      `the day the incident started` IS A DATE
      `the day the incident ended` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A `how long I must keep the documentation`
`how long I must keep it under Measure 9.4` s `the date of the documentation` `the day the incident started` `the day the incident ended` MEANS
    CONSIDER `whether the Chapter binds me` s
    WHEN `the Chapter does not bind me, because I am not a Signatory`
        THEN `no retention duty, because the Chapter does not bind me`
    WHEN `the Chapter is not relevant here, because the model is not a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk`
        THEN `no retention duty, because the model is not a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk`
    WHEN `the Chapter binds me` THEN
        `keep it at least until` WITH
            `the day, if the incident's date is the day it started` IS
                `the retention runs until` `the date of the documentation` `the day the incident started`
            `the day, if the incident's date is the day it ended` IS
                CONSIDER `the day the incident ended`
                WHEN NOTHING THEN `the retention runs until` `the date of the documentation` `the day the incident started`
                WHEN JUST ended THEN `the retention runs until` `the date of the documentation` ended

§ `Glossary terms Commitment 9 uses and this encoding does not compute`

-- 'near miss' appears in Measure 9.2, point (9) only as an example of a pattern to
-- report; nothing is computed from it.
-- src:1270 | ‘near miss’ a situation in which a serious incident could have, but ultimately did not,
-- src:1271 | materialise.
--
-- 'systemic risk' is not in the Glossary; Appendix 1 quotes the AI Act's definition, and
-- Recital (i) (src:149) refers to it without quoting it.
-- src:1388 | Article 3(65) AI Act: ‘systemic risk’ means a risk that is specific to the high-impact capabilities of general-
-- src:1389 | purpose AI models, having a significant impact on the Union market due to their reach, or due to actual
-- src:1390 | or reasonably foreseeable negative effects on public health, safety, public security, fundamental rights,
-- src:1391 | or the society as a whole, that can be propagated at scale across the value chain;
